    a: "Non-operating income and expenses, traditionally called fixed charges: rent (on leased land, buildings or equipment), property and other taxes, insurance on the property and owner-level costs such as asset management fees, net of any non-operating income like a rooftop antenna lease. Subtracting them from income after management fees gives EBITDA.",
